      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm not a medical professional, but I can offer general guidance. It's great that you're considering your health, and low potassium (hypokalemia) can cause muscle cramps and fatigue, especially in people with kidney disease. However, taking potassium supplements requires careful consideration due to your kidney disease. Consult your doctor before starting any supplements, as they can help you determine the best course of action and recommend dosages that won't overburden your kidneys.",
